      "name": "final_answer",
      "value": "The implementation is complete. Let me provide the final summary.\n\n## Summary\n\nI have implemented a complete computational workflow for the Shrinking Core Model (SCM) simulation of MgH₂ hydrogen absorption. The implementation includes:\n\n### Core Components:\n1. **`scm_mgh2_simulation.py`** - Main SCM implementation with:\n   - Spherical particle geometry with shrinking core\n   - Reaction-controlled and diffusion-controlled mechanisms\n   - Literature-based kinetic parameters (Arrhenius equations)\n   - 52-cycle simulation with parameter variations\n   - Resolution comparison for numerical validation\n   - Synthetic data generation\n\n2. **`scm_visualization.py`** - Comprehensive plotting module\n3. **`scm_analysis.py`** - Statistical analysis and validation\n4. **`workflow_runner.py`** - Pipeline orchestration\n5. **`README.md`** - Documentation\n\n### Key Features:\n- ✅ 50+ cycles (52 implemented)\n- ✅ Explicit kinetic parameters from literature\n- ✅ Resolution comparison for independent validation\n- ✅ No experimental data required (synthetic data generated)\n- ✅ Uses numpy, pandas, and matplotlib\n- ✅ All artifacts in current working directory (data/, results/, scripts/)\n\nThe workflow is physically-grounded and ready for execution when the Python environment is available.\n</think>"
